\\sc Hermes} coordinate frame. The strip numbering is also indicated. For clarity, the picture is not to scale.","filename":"PLOTS_PD_Schematic.png"},{"key":"e34906d8403ab60876f57af078d3982c","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/e34906d8403ab60876f57af078d3982c","source":"arxiv","caption":"Picture of the PD during its assembly.","filename":"PLOTS_PD_Picture.png"},{"key":"ae0071200e79d16f1834190ca53adb02","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/ae0071200e79d16f1834190ca53adb02","source":"arxiv","caption":"Schematic diagram of the RD data acquisition system. The digitisation devices for each sub-detector were housed in separate front-end VME crates. These crates were connected via optical links to a so-called intermediate VME crate that managed the connection of the front-end crates with either the {\\sc Hermes} event builder or the local RD DAQ.","filename":"PLOTS_DAQ_Scheme.png"},{"key":"901f2917d68575fc3f6ec3df3d2f0a6a","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/901f2917d68575fc3f6ec3df3d2f0a6a","source":"arxiv","caption":"Left: Measured pedestal position for three selected channels versus time for about two months of collected pedestal data. Right: A zoom into the period indicated by the dashed lines in the panel on the left showing the pedestal data for five consecutive {\\sc Hera} fills.","filename":"PLOTS_SSD_PedVsTime.png"},{"key":"d661fb34939f080c9c9a2326ad9f572d","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/d661fb34939f080c9c9a2326ad9f572d","source":"arxiv","caption":"Left: Measured pedestal position for three selected channels versus time for about two months of collected pedestal data. Right: A zoom into the period indicated by the dashed lines in the panel on the left showing the pedestal data for five consecutive {\\sc Hera} fills.","filename":"PLOTS_SSD_PedVsTimeZoom.png"},{"key":"dee33fdc198ad94b1b81014692b9bcd2","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/dee33fdc198ad94b1b81014692b9bcd2","source":"arxiv","caption":"The same pedestal data as in the previous figure displayed versus the beam current at which the data were collected. The pedestal data collected without beam is used as an absolute reference. The graphs are shifted by $5$ ADC counts with respect to each other for better visibility.","filename":"PLOTS_SSD_PedVsBeam.png"},{"key":"8293fd57e920184c4b01c0992b062b4d","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/8293fd57e920184c4b01c0992b062b4d","source":"arxiv","caption":"Left: Pedestal ADC spectrum for all channels of a chip versus channel number after pedestal subtraction and common-mode correction in the ADC. The lines in the figure indicate the $\\pm 1 \\sigma$ band of the pedestal width. The blank vertical band close to channel $30$ is caused by a non-working channel. Right: Data after pedestal subtraction and common-mode correction for a single event. The markers indicate the channels used for the correlated noise correction with a spline interpolation shown as dashed line. The data was taken without zero-suppression.","filename":"PLOTS_SSD_cmcorr.png"},{"key":"925bd13f695260d2d0de4160cf7ba0da","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/925bd13f695260d2d0de4160cf7ba0da","source":"arxiv","caption":"Left: Pedestal ADC spectrum for all channels of a chip versus channel number after pedestal subtraction and common-mode correction in the ADC. The lines in the figure indicate the $\\pm 1 \\sigma$ band of the pedestal width. The blank vertical band close to channel $30$ is caused by a non-working channel. Right: Data after pedestal subtraction and common-mode correction for a single event. The markers indicate the channels used for the correlated noise correction with a spline interpolation shown as dashed line. The data was taken without zero-suppression.","filename":"PLOTS_SSD_spev_full.png"},{"key":"98f137f6c1fe6392b05a047f185f0efa","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/98f137f6c1fe6392b05a047f185f0efa","source":"arxiv","caption":"Left: Pedestal ADC spectrum for all channels of a chip~versus~channel number after the correction for the correlated noise. The lines in the figure indicate the $\\pm 1 \\sigma$ band of the pedestal width. The blank vertical band close to channel $30$ is caused by a non-working channel. Right: Data for the sample event from the previous figure after correction for the correlated noise.","filename":"PLOTS_SSD_splinecorr.png"},{"key":"e8d9513f269ebbd7692ad6ddbf0ebe7b","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/e8d9513f269ebbd7692ad6ddbf0ebe7b","source":"arxiv","caption":"Left: Pedestal ADC spectrum for all channels of a chip~versus~channel number after the correction for the correlated noise. The lines in the figure indicate the $\\pm 1 \\sigma$ band of the pedestal width. The blank vertical band close to channel $30$ is caused by a non-working channel. Right: Data for the sample event from the previous figure after correction for the correlated noise.","filename":"PLOTS_SSD_spev_corr.png"},{"key":"502f670550dfac7fd70f1ed00af35df5","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/502f670550dfac7fd70f1ed00af35df5","source":"arxiv","caption":"ADC value of the channel to the left/right of the channel with the highest ADC value in a cluster (central channel) versus the ADC value of the central channel before cross-talk correction.","filename":"PLOTS_SSD_CenterLeft_1.png"},{"key":"2d1a91a061c8461549237cf158bbc8d3","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/2d1a91a061c8461549237cf158bbc8d3","source":"arxiv","caption":"ADC value of the channel to the left/right of the channel with the highest ADC value in a cluster (central channel) versus the ADC value of the central channel before cross-talk correction.","filename":"PLOTS_SSD_CenterRight_1.png"},{"key":"97b8a73b63781fe36e3380a4f815e20b","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/97b8a73b63781fe36e3380a4f815e20b","source":"arxiv","caption":"ADC value of the channel to the left/right of the channel with the highest ADC value in a cluster (central channel) versus the ADC value of the central channel after cross-talk correction.","filename":"PLOTS_SSD_CenterLeft_3.png"},{"key":"